"Dquarkus.native.container-build=true` uses volume mounts to make the JAR "
"available in the build container, but volume mounts do not work with remote "
"daemons. The remote container build driver copies the necessary files "
"instead of mounting them. Note that even though the remote driver also works "
"with local daemons, the local driver should be preferred in the local case "
"because mounting is usually more performant than copying."
msgstr ""

